# RSF06-01: rules & setup, and the tester.
title The rules page shows every rule in plain words with how often it decided, and the tester shows what happens to any address, step by step
row  addr:box "An address to try" "GET /wp-login.php" | steps:warnbox "Every check, in order" "✓ fine, ✕ refused here" | verdict:okbox "One sentence" "who decides, and why"
row  rules:box "Every rule" "its ID, its line, its count" | settings:box "Every setting" "the secret only as set"
arrow addr -> steps "nothing counted"
arrow steps -> verdict go
arrow verdict -> rules "links to its row"
note The same check on the command line: request-shield trace site.rules "GET https://…".
